  "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
  "instance_name": "general_custer_stereotype",
  "label": "General Custer as a symbol of military aggression and failure",
  "description": "General Custer is often stereotyped in popular culture as a reckless, arrogant, and ultimately doomed military leader whose actions led to the defeat of the U.S. Army at Little Bighorn. This stereotype is leveraged in the meme to imply that the figure in the image represents a violent, aggressive force, which is then used to express hatred toward both banks and Native Americans. The meme relies on the public perception of Custer as a symbol of military failure and aggression to convey its message.",
